// Task: ZP-TBD-18, P-2 (reschedule trip) + P-3 (reschedule billing + Task for Shirley)
// Zoho App: CRM
// Module: Operations -> Trips, Sales_Orders, Tasks
// Function Name: automation.handleAutopsyReschedule (NEW)
// Trigger Source: NEW Workflow Rule on Operations, field update on Reschedule_Reason,
//                  criteria: Reschedule_Reason is not empty. Argument mapping: crmid =
//                  Related_Deal.id (the Operations record's linked Deal).
//
// Andrea, 2026-08-14, verbatim (resolving the only real open question on P-2): "You have
// the entire logic for an autopsy trip. The deceased gets picked up from morgue location
// they are at and is transported to an autopsy location. a reschedule brings them back to
// the morgue and back to the autopsy location on a reschedule."
//
// WHAT THIS CONFIRMS: the live template function createTripOnTheDayOfAutopsyDateWithTask
// (pulled 2026-08-14) already branches on Is_Deceased_In_Our_Care -- Scenario A (pickup =
// DFH's own Kingston/Mobay location, destination = autopsy facility) vs Scenario B (the
// reverse). A reschedule can only happen AFTER the deceased has already been picked up once
// (that's the entire premise of a no-show/frozen-body reschedule -- the body is already
// back in DFH's storage), so Is_Deceased_In_Our_Care is always "Yes" by the time a
// reschedule fires. This is exactly Andrea's description: pickup from DFH storage ("the
// morgue"), destination = autopsy facility -- Scenario A, unconditionally, for this flow.
// No decision was actually needed here -- the existing template already has the answer.
//
// SCOPE NOTE (deliberately narrow, per Andrea: "you can only build what is absolutely
// clear"): this function creates the reschedule Trip and adds the Reschedule Trip fee line
// item + the Task for Ms. Shirley -- the three pieces the requirement docs state
// unambiguously. It does NOT independently recompute or touch the Police Cases Sales
// Order's STORAGE line item -- that is already maintained by the existing LNI (P-1) and
// autopsy-completed storage functions, which continue to run off their own date fields
// regardless of a reschedule. Duplicating that logic here risked fighting with those
// functions over the same line item. If Andrea/Shirley confirm a reschedule needs its own
// distinct storage adjustment beyond what those functions already do, that's a follow-up,
// not assumed here.
//
// Branches on Operations.Reschedule_Reason (set by the Driver App via
// Save_Autopsy_Disposition, per ZP-TBD-1/FUNCTION_SOURCES.md FN-5 area):
//   - "Autopsy not done" (no-show): create/update the reschedule Trip, add the Reschedule
//     Trip fee to the Police SO, create the Task for Ms. Shirley.
//   - "Problem caused by DFH" (e.g. frozen): does NOTHING -- no trip, no billing, no task.
//     DFH absorbs the cost and nothing gets scheduled (confirmed by live test 2026-08-15;
//     the original assumption that a trip should still be created here was WRONG).
//   - "X-ray required" (P-4, added 2026-08-15): create/update an X-ray trip (same Scenario
//     A pickup/destination clone as the reschedule trip), add the SAME Reschedule Trip fee
//     product to the Police SO. No Task -- unlike a no-show, an X-ray is billed to the
//     institution automatically with no officer/family ambiguity to sort out.
// Forensics/IFSL is never billed here, in any branch (not touched).
//
// P-4 PRODUCT DECISION (Andrea, 2026-08-15, via the user): use the SAME Reschedule Trip
// product (6503357000004300032) for the X-ray trip fee, rather than any of the three
// CRH-specific radiology products (CRH- Radiology West / CRH Pickup @ NC Imaging /
// Transport to PME). This was the user's call, explicitly to be raised with Andrea in the
// next comment note for her to confirm or correct -- flag this in the completion
// report/comment note, do not treat it as fully settled.
//
// P-4 SETUP NEEDED BEFORE DEPLOY: Trips.Trip_Type has NO "X-ray"-type value today (checked
// live 2026-08-15 -- full picklist pulled, nothing matches). This function uses a new value
// "X-Ray Trip" -- add it to the Trip_Type picklist (Setup > Customization > Modules and
// Fields > Trips > Trip_Type) before deploying, or this record create will fail.
//
// P-4 NOT INCLUDED: the three new radiology fields from PH_Billing_Requirements_FINAL.md
// (X_Ray_Date, Radiology_Location, X_Ray_Completed_Date) do not exist on Deals yet, so this
// function cannot route the trip's destination to a radiology-specific location -- it reuses
// the same Autopsy_Locations facility as the reschedule trip instead, as an interim default.
// Once those fields exist, Destination_Street_Address/City for the X-ray branch should be
// updated to read from Radiology_Location instead of Autopsy_Locations.
//
// LIVE TEST FIXES (2026-08-15), all applied below:
//   1. Task owner was the Deal's Owner -- wrong. Must be Caeren Shirley specifically
//      (user id 6503357000009256001, cas@dfhja.com), hardcoded.
//   2. Task creation was not idempotent -- a second reschedule on the same Deal would
//      create a second task. Now searches for an existing task on the same Deal + Subject
//      first and reuses it instead of duplicating.
//   3. "Problem caused by DFH" was creating a trip -- confirmed wrong by live test. This
//      reason now returns immediately with no trip, no billing, no task.
//
// P-1/P-2/P-3 are deployed and confirmed passing live (2026-08-15). P-4 (this round's
// addition) is NOT yet deployed -- needs the Trip_Type picklist value added first, then a
// live test with Reschedule_Reason = "X-ray required".

void automation.handleAutopsyReschedule(Int crmid)
{
	dealDetails = invokeurl
	[
		url :"https://www.zohoapis.com/crm/v7/Deals/" + crmid
		type :GET
		connection:"zohooauth"
	];
	recordInfo = dealDetails.get("data").get(0);

	opsCriteria = "(Related_Deal:equals:" + crmid + ")";
	opsRecords = zoho.crm.searchRecords("Operations",opsCriteria,1,1);
	rescheduleReason = "";
	for each op in opsRecords
	{
		rescheduleReason = ifnull(op.get("Reschedule_Reason"),"");
		break;
	}

	if(rescheduleReason == "Problem caused by DFH")
	{
		// FIX (live test, 2026-08-15): confirmed no trip should be created at all for this
		// reason -- DFH absorbs the cost and nothing gets scheduled.
		return;
	}
	if(rescheduleReason != "Autopsy not done" && rescheduleReason != "X-ray required")
	{
		// Anything else (empty, unrecognized value) -- do nothing.
		return;
	}
	isXray = (rescheduleReason == "X-ray required");

	// ===== Trip creation -- clones createTripOnTheDayOfAutopsyDateWithTask's Scenario A =====
	// (pickup = DFH location, destination = autopsy facility), since a reschedule/X-ray trip
	// always finds the deceased already in DFH's care. See header note above.
	tripTypeValue = "Autopsy Reschedule";
	createdMarker = "Autopsy_Reschedule";
	tripNameValue = "Autopsy Reschedule Trip";
	if(isXray)
	{
		tripTypeValue = "X-Ray Trip";
		createdMarker = "X_Ray_Trip";
		tripNameValue = "X-Ray Trip";
	}

	trips = zoho.crm.getRelatedRecords("Trips","Deals",crmid);
	tripAvailable = false;
	tripId = null;
	for each trip in trips
	{
		if(trip.get("Trip_Type") == tripTypeValue && trip.get("Created_on_This_Field_Update") == createdMarker)
		{
			tripId = trip.get("id");
			tripAvailable = true;
			break;
		}
	}

	tripMap = Map();
	opsCriteria2 = "(Related_Deal:equals:" + crmid + ")";
	opsRecords2 = zoho.crm.searchRecords("Operations",opsCriteria2,1,1);
	for each op in opsRecords2
	{
		if(ifnull(op.get("id"),"") != "")
		{
			opsLocation = ifnull(op.get("Location"),"");
			if(opsLocation == "Kingston")
			{
				tripMap.put("Pickup_Street_Address","20A W. Kings House Rd.");
				tripMap.put("Pickup_City","Kingston");
			}
			else if(opsLocation == "Montego Bay")
			{
				tripMap.put("Pickup_Street_Address","45 Union St.");
				tripMap.put("Pickup_City","Montego Bay");
			}
			else if(opsLocation != "")
			{
				tripMap.put("Pickup_Street_Address",opsLocation);
				tripMap.put("Pickup_City","Montego Bay");
			}
			break;
		}
	}
	if(!isNull(recordInfo.get("Autopsy_Locations")))
	{
		try
		{
			autopsyAcct = zoho.crm.getRecordById("Accounts",recordInfo.get("Autopsy_Locations").get("id"));
			tripMap.put("Destination_Street_Address",ifnull(autopsyAcct.get("Billing_Street"),""));
			tripMap.put("Destination_City",ifnull(autopsyAcct.get("Billing_City"),""));
			locMap = Map();
			locMap.put("id",recordInfo.get("Autopsy_Locations").get("id"));
			tripMap.put("Autopsy_Location",locMap);
		}
		catch (eAcct)
		{
		}
	}

	if(tripAvailable == false)
	{
		tripMap.put("Name",tripNameValue);
		tripMap.put("Trip_Type",tripTypeValue);
		// FIX (2026-08-15): was "DO NOT SCHEDULE", copied from createTripOnTheDayOfAutopsyDateWithTask's
		// template without also copying the mechanism that releases it from that status.
		// "Autopsy Initial" trips get released via two workflow-triggered functions,
		// groupAutopsyTrips and cascadeAutopsyParentStatus, which key specifically off
		// Trip_Type == "Autopsy Initial" / "Multi Deceased Autopsy Trip" -- neither fires
		// for "Autopsy Reschedule" or "X-Ray Trip", so a trip created with DO NOT SCHEDULE
		// here would stay stuck in that status forever, permanently invisible in Trip
		// Manager (which unconditionally excludes DO NOT SCHEDULE trips from every view).
		// "Requested" is the correct starting status -- same as any other newly created
		// trip needing a driver/vehicle assignment, and it already feeds the existing
		// "Change Status to Scheduled when Driver and Vehicle Assigned" workflow.
		tripMap.put("Trip_Status","Requested");
		tripMap.put("Deal",crmid);
		tripMap.put("Created_on_This_Field_Update",createdMarker);
		tripMap.put("Owner",recordInfo.get("Owner").get("id"));
		tripCreationResult = zoho.crm.createRecord("Trips",tripMap,{"trigger":{"workflow"}});
		info tripCreationResult;
		tripAccountRelation = Map();
		tripAccountRelation.put("Trips",tripCreationResult.get("id"));
		tripAccountRelation.put("Related_Account_Record",recordInfo.get("Account_Name").get("id"));
		zoho.crm.createRecord("Trips_Accounts_Relation",tripAccountRelation);
		dealMap = Map();
		dealMap.put("Trips",tripCreationResult.get("id"));
		zoho.crm.updateRecord("Deals",crmid,dealMap);
	}
	else
	{
		zoho.crm.updateRecord("Trips",tripId,tripMap,{"trigger":{"workflow"}});
	}

	// ===== From here down: rescheduleReason is "Autopsy not done" or "X-ray required" =====
	// ("Problem caused by DFH" and anything else already returned above). Both reasons bill
	// the same Reschedule Trip fee to the Police SO; only "Autopsy not done" also creates
	// the Task for Shirley (see the isXray guard below the billing block).

	// Add the Reschedule Trip fee to the Police Cases Sales Order (add-or-update pattern,
	// matches the existing patchAutopsyTripQuantityOnSalesOrder / patchPickupQuantityOnSalesOrder
	// convention in ZP-TBD-6). Used for BOTH "Autopsy not done" and "X-ray required" -- see
	// the P-4 product decision note in the header.
	rescheduleTripProductId = "6503357000004300032"; // Reschedule Trip, per DEVELOPER_BUILD_DOC.md §0
	salesOrders = standalone.COQLQuery("select Subject from Sales_Orders where Deal_Name = '" + crmid + "' and Sales_Order_Type = 'Police Cases' limit 1");
	if(salesOrders.size() > 0)
	{
		salesOrderDetails = invokeurl
		[
			url :"https://www.zohoapis.com/crm/v7/Sales_Orders/" + salesOrders.toList().get(0).get("id")
			type :GET
			connection:"zohooauth"
		];
		salesOrderInfo = salesOrderDetails.get("data").get(0);
		lineItemList = list();
		if(salesOrderInfo.get("Ordered_Items").size() > 0)
		{
			lineItemList = salesOrderInfo.get("Ordered_Items");
		}
		productDetails = zoho.crm.getRecordById("Products",rescheduleTripProductId.toLong());
		existingIndex = -1;
		for each item in lineItemList
		{
			if(item.contains("Product_Name"))
			{
				productName = item.get("Product_Name");
				if(productName != null && productName.contains("id") && productName.get("id") == rescheduleTripProductId)
				{
					existingIndex = lineItemList.indexOf(item);
					break;
				}
			}
		}
		if(existingIndex >= 0)
		{
			existingItem = lineItemList.get(existingIndex);
			existingQty = ifnull(existingItem.get("Quantity"),0);
			existingItem.put("Quantity",existingQty + 1); // each reschedule adds one more trip fee
			lineItemList.remove(existingIndex);
			lineItemList.add(existingItem);
		}
		else
		{
			productMap = Map();
			productMap.put("Product_Name",rescheduleTripProductId);
			productMap.put("Quantity",1);
			productMap.put("List_Price",productDetails.get("Unit_Price"));
			lineItemList.add(productMap);
		}
		salesOrderMap = Map();
		salesOrderMap.put("Ordered_Items",lineItemList);
		recordList = list();
		recordList.add(salesOrderMap);
		dataMap = Map();
		dataMap.put("data",recordList);
		updateSalesOrder = invokeurl
		[
			url :"https://www.zohoapis.com/crm/v2.1/Sales_Orders/" + salesOrders.toList().get(0).get("id")
			type :PUT
			parameters:dataMap.toString()
			connection:"zohooauth"
		];
		info updateSalesOrder;
		standalone.createInvoiceBasedOnSalesOrderForPolice(crmid);
	}

	if(isXray)
	{
		// X-ray is billed straight to the institution automatically -- no officer/family
		// ambiguity to sort out, so no Task for Shirley here (unlike the no-show path below).
		return;
	}

	// Task for Ms. Shirley -- manual invoice, since the system can't reliably tell
	// officer-no-show from family-no-show (Andrea's design decision, confirmed 2026-08-13).
	// FIX (live test, 2026-08-15): owner is Caeren Shirley specifically (id
	// 6503357000009256001, cas@dfhja.com), not the Deal's owner. Also: idempotent -- if a
	// task for this exact Deal + Subject already exists, do NOT create a second one; a
	// re-fire of the same reschedule reason on the same Deal must reuse the existing task,
	// not spawn a duplicate.
	taskSubject = "Raise manual reschedule invoice -- decide police-officer vs family charge";
	existingTaskCriteria = "(What_Id:equals:" + crmid + ")and(Subject:equals:" + taskSubject + ")";
	existingTasks = List();
	try
	{
		existingTasks = zoho.crm.searchRecords("Tasks",existingTaskCriteria,1,1);
	}
	catch (eTaskSearch)
	{
		existingTasks = List();
	}
	if(existingTasks.size() == 0)
	{
		taskMap = Map();
		taskMap.put("Subject",taskSubject);
		taskMap.put("$se_module","Deals");
		taskMap.put("What_Id",crmid);
		taskMap.put("Owner","6503357000009256001"); // Caeren Shirley
		taskMap.put("Due_Date",zoho.currentdate.addDay(2));
		taskMap.put("Status","Not Started");
		taskMap.put("Send_Notification_Email",true);
		taskMap.put("Task_Type","Reschedule Manual Invoice");
		createTask = zoho.crm.createRecord("Tasks",taskMap);
		info createTask;
	}
	else
	{
		info "Task already exists for this Deal (" + existingTasks.get(0).get("id") + ") -- not creating a duplicate.";
	}
}
